  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the probability of the maximum outcome and prefers the lottery with the lower such probability (i.e., disfavors high chances of the highest payoff). In this case, the reason would favor Lottery A (max outcome 2500 at 33%) over B (max outcome 2400 at 100%). However, the individual chooses B because of its certainty, not because of a low probability of the maximum outcome. The individual’s reasoning is based on risk aversion and preference for sure outcomes, not on evaluating the probability of the maximum outcome as defined by the reason. There is no mention or consideration of the 'probability of the maximum outcome' as a comparative metric. Thus, while both the reason and the individual might end up favoring a lottery with a lower chance of the highest outcome, the underlying logic differs fundamentally. The individual does not use the specific comparison required by the reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 20
}

